  "rating": {
    "inherent": "low",
    "residual": "low",
    "forecast": "moderate",
    "rationale": "Reviewed artifacts show a narrow HR policy QA agent with one read-only search tool over internal published policies and a single session-bound chat reply path. Present attack paths remain low because the only user input is trusted employee chat, the reply sink is limited to the authenticated requester, and verified network-layer egress denial removes external exfiltration channels. Forecast rises to moderate if network egress is later enabled or a new outbound tool is added, because the current low rating depends on the absence of any attacker-reachable egress sink. Validation was performed manually from the provided schema and checklist because scripts could not be run in this environment."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "This assessment reflects the declared design and configuration in prompt.md, tools.json, and runtime notes, not observed runtime behavior.",
    "No runtime configuration artifact, network policy file, or audit log sample was provided, so control verification is limited to the declarations in the runtime notes except where the notes explicitly state a pen test verified egress denial.",
    "No source code or chat platform configuration was provided, so session binding, SSO enforcement, and exact logging semantics were not independently verified."
  ]
